WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.903
[music playing] (SINGING)
[non-english speech]

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.338
ANNA COREN: An Iranian love
song plays from a cassette,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.776
as a driver navigates his way
through the snow-dusted Lehman

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:13.079
Valley in northwestern
Afghanistan.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.047
Crammed in the back
of his station wagon

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:18.117
is a mother and
her six children,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.719
who've just left behind a
life of constant struggle

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.324
and hardship, all
they've ever known.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.494
Among them,
nine-year-old Parwana.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:32.031
Our cameraman, Siddiqui,
asks her how she's feeling.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:35.668
I'm so happy, she says,
with a beaming smile.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.671
CNN met Parwana,
dressed in pink,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.940
in an internally
displaced camp in Bagdi's

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.709
province back in October.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.544
Her father claims
he was selling her

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.448
to feed the rest of the family.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:52.351
As a humanitarian crisis
grips the country,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.521
he'd already sold his
12-year-old into marriage,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:59.058
and told CNN that unless
his situation improved,

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:02.328
he would have to sell his four
remaining daughters as well,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:06.465
including the
youngest, just two.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.167 line:8%
"If I didn't have these
daughters to sell,"

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:11.604 line:14%
he asks, "what should I do?"

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.106
Parwana's buyer, who
lived in a nearby village,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:20.079
confirmed he was taking the
9-year-old as his second wife.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.881
INTERPRETER: I'm 55 years old.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.751
I have a wife with four
daughters and a son.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.485
I bought her for myself.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.221
I will wait until
she becomes older.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.024
ANNA COREN: CNN was
granted rare access to film

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.527
the final payment and handover.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.395
The buyer asked for
it to take place

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.032
at a house in his
village, and not the camp,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.000
for security reasons.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.703
He paid a total of
200,000 Afghanis,

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:50.676
just over $2000 for Parwana,
in land, sheep and cash.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.712 line:8%
This is your bride,
please take care of her.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.781
Says Parwana's father.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:58.951
Of course, I will take care
of her, replies the man.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.085
[non-english speech]

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.388
ANNA COREN: As he drags
her away, she whimpers.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.997
Moments later, she digs
her heels into the dirt,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:17.269
refusing to go,
but it's hopeless.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.806
CNN's story caused an outcry.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.575
- And a distressing story
out of Afghanistan, showing--

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.011
ANNA COREN: The network was
inundated with offers of help

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:28.114
from the public aid
organizations and NGOs

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.416
wanting to assist Parwana
and the other girls

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.784
featured in our story.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:35.555
The US-based charity, Too
Young To Wed, took the lead.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.624
Its founding executive
director, Stephanie Sinclair,

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.626
has been working to
end child marriage

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.764
and help vulnerable girls around
the world for almost 20 years.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:48.267
She says the perfect storm
is brewing in Afghanistan,

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.602
and it's the girls
that are suffering.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.738
STEPHANIE SINCLAIR: I know these
stories are difficult to watch,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.740
and they're difficult
to do, and they

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.642
bring around a lot of concern.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.445
But at the same time, we need
to keep people understanding

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.446
that this is happening.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:02.281
We need to keep
ringing the alarm bell,

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.051
to understand these are
real girls and real lives,

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:07.253
and they can be changed.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.621
ANNA COREN: Within
Bagdi's province,

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.490
there was widespread backlash
towards Parwana's father

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:15.127
and the buyer after our story
went to air, with claims they'd

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.396
brought shame on the community.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:22.068
Even the Taliban told CNN
the practice is forbidden.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.536
INTERPRETER: I request everyone
not to sell their children.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.840
Child marriage is not a good
thing, and we condemn it.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.142
ANNA COREN: Women's
rights activist,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.477
and US citizen,
Mahbouba Seraj, who

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:34.314
chose to stay in Kabul after
the Taliban swept to power

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.950
in August to run
her women's shelter,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.586
says Parwana's case is just
the tip of the iceberg.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.887
MAHBOUBA SERAJ: It
is a lot of misery.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.589
There is a lot of mistreatment.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:47.126
There is a lot of abuse is
involved in these things.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.495
And it will keep on
happening with the hunger,

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:52.198
with the winter, with poverty.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.766
ANNA COREN: As a result
of the controversy

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.736
caused by the story, an
intervention from the charity,

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:00.139
Parwana was allowed to return
home after almost two weeks

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.573
with the buyer's family.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.741
[non-english speech]

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.310
ANNA COREN: "Since
Parwana has been rescued,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.014
I'm very happy for that,"
says Pawana's father.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:11.584
He admitted to CNN that under
duress from the community

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.786
and some local media outlets.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.522
He changed his story out
of embarrassment for what

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:19.659
he had done, and apologized.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.027
The buyer is
unreachable for comment,

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:25.231
but the debt is
still outstanding.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.501
Too Young to Wed then organized
to have Parwana, her mother,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.736
and siblings removed
from the camp

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.939
with the father's permission.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.842
The four-hour journey to
neighboring Herat province

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:43.616
was broken up with
some childhood fun

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.251
before arriving at the motel.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.554
For children who've only
ever lived in a tent,

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:53.159
the novelty of being warm, fed
and safe wasn't wearing off.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:56.862
[non-english speech]

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:57.963
ANNA COREN: "They rescued me.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.233
They've given me a new
life," says Parwana.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:03.035
"I thank the charity
for helping me."

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.706
A few days later, they
moved into the safe house.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.575
Parwana's mother,
27-year-old Reza Gul,

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.310
has never lived in a house.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.612
She was sold into
marriage at 13,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.949
and has since had seven
children, six of whom

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.183
were girls.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.786
Most days in the camp,
she would beg for food,

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.790
and often her family
would go to sleep hungry.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:28.026
Now all she wants is to give
her children a better life.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.395
[non-english speech]

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.464
"I have a dream, a
wish, to go to school

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.632
and start an
education," she says.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:36.468
"I have a lot of
wishes for then."

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.303 line:8%
Too Young to Wed
has already begun

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:43.409 line:8%
distributing aid to Parwana's
impoverished camp among others.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.512
While the small charity is
prepared to bridge the gap,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:50.015
they're calling on the large
aid organizations to step up.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.383
STEPHANIE SINCLAIR:
These are communities

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.186
that have relied on
international aid

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.054
for the last 20 years.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.590
And so, with a lot
of that aid stopping,

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.625
these people didn't
stop needing support.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:03.295
We can't let them pay the
price, because ultimately girls

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.364
always pay the biggest price.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.166
ANNA COREN: I speak
to Parwana on Zoom,

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.535
through my colleague Bassir.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.638
Hello Parwana, I'm Anna.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:13.705
[non-english speech]

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.540
INTERPRETER: How are you?

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.675
How are you feeling?

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:16.976
ANNA COREN: I'm very
good, thank you.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:18.177
How are you?

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.046
[non-english speech]

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.548
INTERPRETER: I'm fine.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.449
I'm so happy.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.587
I'm safe.

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:30.022
I rescued.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:34.527
ANNA COREN: Then she asks, "When
are you sending me to school?"

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.697
She wants to study and
become a doctor or a teacher,

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.733
but fairy-tale endings are
few and far between for girls

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:41.934
in Afghanistan.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.470
Even more so now than ever.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.340
Anna Coren, CNN.

